   "stem": {
      "text": "Let F be the antiderivative of \\( f(x) = \\frac{x^{2}}{x^{3} + 1} \\) on the interval \\( x > -1 \\) with \\( F(1) = 1 \\). Find the exact value of \\( F\\left(2\\right) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Ln",
               [
                  "Rational",
                  9,
                  2
               ]
            ],
            3
         ],
         1
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x^{3} + 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               3
            ],
            1
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then \\( du = 3 x^{2} \\, dx \\), so \\( x^{2} \\, dx = \\frac{1}{3} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Since \\( F(2) = F(1) + \\int_{1}^{2} \\frac{x^{2}}{x^{3} + 1} \\, dx \\), convert the limits: \\( x = 1 \\) gives \\( u = 2 \\) and \\( x = 2 \\) gives \\( u = 9 \\), so the integral becomes \\( \\int_{2}^{9} \\frac{1}{3 u} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            1,
            [
               "Multiply",
               3,
               "u"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "An antiderivative of \\( \\frac{1}{3 u} \\) is \\( \\frac{\\ln{\\left(u \\right)}}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Ln",
               "u"
            ],
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "The integral is \\( \\frac{\\ln{\\left(9 \\right)}}{3} - \\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{3}\\right) = \\frac{\\ln{\\left(\\frac{9}{2} \\right)}}{3} \\), so \\( F(2) = 1 + \\frac{\\ln{\\left(\\frac{9}{2} \\right)}}{3} = \\frac{\\ln{\\left(\\frac{9}{2} \\right)}}{3} + 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
